                <pb facs="1042" n="926" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg926"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.51A/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dunn</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-06-28T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 28, 1923—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>70. For General Russell.</p>
                <p>Your 85, June 26, 1 p.m.</p>
                <p>When Hord presents his resignation you may say to President Borno if inquiry is
                    made, that Department has no objection to its acceptance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
